      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of the following geometric sequence.\n\n$$\n10,\\,-4,\\,\\frac{8}{5},\\,…\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=10$ and the second term is ${a}_{2}=-4,$ so we can find the common ratio, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-4}{10}=-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the common ratio is $r=-\\frac{2}{5},$  we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =10\\cdot {(-\\frac{2}{5})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
